<%# The front door, written like a marketing page for someone who hasn't played with Grimwilder yet: the hero with an example of play, how it works, the table and the sheets each beside a picture of them, the free tools, then the buttons again. The examples are made of the app's own dice and chat styles; they're illustrations, not live data. %>
<div class="home">
  <section class="home-hero">
    <div class="home-hero__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">A play toolkit for Grimwild: Community Edition</p>
      <h1 class="home-hero__title">Grimwilder</h1>
      <p class="home-hero__tagline">Keep the dice honest and the story moving.</p>
      <p class="home-hero__lede">
        Grimwilder keeps track of your Grimwild game, from the pools and spark to who took harm, so the table can stay in the story.
        The GM runs the session from one screen, every player's sheet rolls its own dice,
        and everyone shares one log of what happened.
      </p>
      <%= render "pages/cta" %>
    </div>

    <figure class="showcase" aria-label="An example of play: the GM's narration, a roll in the shared log, and a pool running down">
      <div class="showcase__bar">
        <span class="showcase__live">Live</span>
        <span>Session 8 · Scene 2, The mill fire</span>
      </div>
      <div class="showcase__feed">
        <p class="showcase__line showcase__line--narration">
          <span class="showcase__who">GM · Cut to</span>
          Smoke pours from the mill as the waterwheel catches.
        </p>
        <p class="showcase__line">
          <span class="showcase__who showcase__who--npc">Old Hesk <small>voiced by GM</small></span>
          “Leave the grain! The roof's coming down!”
        </p>
        <div class="showcase__roll">
          <p class="showcase__who">Tibbs rolls Agility · 3d + 1 spark, 1 thorn</p>
          <div class="showcase__dice">
            <%= render "shared/die", value: 2, size: 32 %>
            <%= render "shared/die", value: 5, size: 32, state: :highest %>
            <%= render "shared/die", value: 3, size: 32 %>
            <%= render "shared/die", value: 4, size: 32, extra: "die--spark" %>
            <%= render "shared/die", value: 6, kind: "d8", size: 32 %>
            <span class="showcase__word">Messy</span>
          </div>
          <p class="showcase__reason">Success, with an impact move.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="showcase__pool">
          <span class="showcase__pool-name"><span class="showcase__pool-size">4d → 2d</span> The roof gives way</span>
          <span class="pool-track" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="pool-track__segment pool-track__segment--full"></span>
            <span class="pool-track__segment pool-track__segment--full"></span>
            <span class="pool-track__segment"></span>
            <span class="pool-track__segment"></span>
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="showcase__line showcase__line--mine">
          <span class="showcase__who">Tibbs</span>
          “Out the window. Now!”
        </p>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="home-steps" aria-labelledby="steps-heading">
    <h2 id="steps-heading" class="visually-hidden">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step__number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <h3 class="step__name">The GM starts a campaign</h3>
        <p class="step__desc">They pitch it, pick the optional rules, and share its invite link with the players.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step__number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <h3 class="step__name">Build the party</h3>
        <p class="step__desc">Everyone makes a character from any of the <%= Grimwild.paths.size %> paths, at any level, and takes a seat.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step__number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        <h3 class="step__name">Play</h3>
        <p class="step__desc">The GM runs scenes and calls for rolls; players roll from their sheets, and it all lands in one log.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="table-heading">
    <header class="home-section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">For the whole table</p>
      <h2 id="table-heading" class="home-section__title">Play at the table</h2>
      <p class="home-section__lede">In the same room or apart, everyone sees the same dice the moment they land.</p>
    </header>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li class="feature">
        <h3 class="feature__name">The GM table</h3>
        <p class="feature__desc">Scenes, suspense, the party's harm and spark at a glance, pools to roll and reveal, and crucibles close by.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="feature">
        <h3 class="feature__name">One shared log</h3>
        <p class="feature__desc">Rolls are made on the server, so everyone sees the same dice. Spark is spent and taken for you, and the GM's secret rolls stay secret.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="feature">
        <h3 class="feature__name">Roll calls</h3>
        <p class="feature__desc">The GM calls for a story roll, a montage or a quarrel, and each player rolls their own dice from wherever they are.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="feature">
        <h3 class="feature__name">Table chat</h3>
        <p class="feature__desc">Narration, NPC voices, in-character lines, table talk and private whispers, side by side with the dice.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="feature">
        <h3 class="feature__name">Sessions and scenes</h3>
        <p class="feature__desc">Start and end them, rest, take downtime. Resets, XP and level-ups are handled, and every session's recap and rolls are kept.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="feature">
        <h3 class="feature__name">Optional rules</h3>
        <p class="feature__desc">Switch on the book's optional rules for a campaign: milestone levels, vigor and armor, encumbrance, tick pools and more.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section home-section--split" aria-labelledby="sheets-heading">
    <figure class="sheet-sample" aria-label="An example stat card: Agility, 3 dice, marked, with 1 of 2 spark">
      <div class="sheet-sample__who">
        <span class="sheet-sample__monogram" aria-hidden="true">T</span>
        <span>
          <span class="sheet-sample__name">Tibbs</span>
          <span class="sheet-sample__meta">Rogue · level 3</span>
        </span>
        <%= render "shared/pips", kind: "spark", value: 1, max: 2 %>
      </div>
      <div class="sheet-sample__stat">
        <span class="sheet-sample__stat-name">Agility</span>
        <span class="sheet-sample__marked">Marked</span>
        <span class="sheet-sample__dice">3d</span>
      </div>
      <p class="sheet-sample__harm">Bloodied · +1t to Brawn and Agility</p>
      <span class="sheet-sample__roll" aria-hidden="true">Roll 3d + 2t</span>
    </figure>

    <div>
      <header class="home-section__head">
        <p class="eyebrow">For every player</p>
        <h2 id="sheets-heading" class="home-section__title">Character sheets that roll</h2>
        <p class="home-section__lede">Your sheet knows your stats, your harm and your talents, and adds them up for you.</p>
      </header>
      <ul class="feature-list feature-list--stacked">
        <li class="feature">
          <h3 class="feature__name">Everything in one roll</h3>
          <p class="feature__desc">Stat dice, spark, assists, thorns from harm and your talents' bonuses add up in one setup, and the result says why it came out that way.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="feature">
          <h3 class="feature__name">Harm and conditions</h3>
          <p class="feature__desc">Marks, bloodied, rattled and desperate, vex, and conditions that count down as pools. The GM can tend them too.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="feature">
          <h3 class="feature__name">Talents that work</h3>
          <p class="feature__desc">Uses to tick, talent pools to roll, choices to make, re-skins, and talents that change a roll after it's made.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="feature">
          <h3 class="feature__name">Arcana</h3>
          <p class="feature__desc">Magic items with their touchstones and power pools, refilled each session, and expendables you use up.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section tool-grid" aria-labelledby="tools-heading">
    <header class="home-section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">No account needed</p>
      <h2 id="tools-heading" class="home-section__title">Free tools</h2>
    </header>
    <ul class="tool-grid__list">
      <li>
        <%= link_to roll_path, class: "tool-card tool-card--ready" do %>
          <span class="tool-card__glyph" aria-hidden="true">d6</span>
          <span class="tool-card__name">Action roll</span>
          <span class="tool-card__desc">Stat dice against thorns. Reads the highest die, applies cuts, calls criticals, and folds in talents like Panache.</span>
        <% end %>
      </li>
      <li>
        <%= link_to crucibles_path, class: "tool-card tool-card--ready" do %>
          <span class="tool-card__glyph" aria-hidden="true"><%= Crucible.all.size %></span>
          <span class="tool-card__name">Crucibles</span>
          <span class="tool-card__desc">The book's tables of evocative words. Roll, smash the results together, and keep the ones you like.</span>
        <% end %>
      </li>
      <li>
        <%= link_to talents_path, class: "tool-card tool-card--ready" do %>
          <span class="tool-card__glyph" aria-hidden="true"><%= Talent.all.reject(&:retired?).size %></span>
          <span class="tool-card__name">Talents</span>
          <span class="tool-card__desc">Every path's talents, plus background, heritage and legacy talents, with a one-line gist of each.</span>
        <% end %>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="home-close" aria-labelledby="close-heading">
    <% if !authenticated? && !Identity.signups_open? %>
      <h2 id="close-heading" class="home-close__title">Want a seat at the table?</h2>
      <p class="home-close__lede">Grimwilder is in a closed beta. Tell us you're interested and we'll be in touch.</p>
      <%= render "pages/cta" %>
    <% else %>
      <h2 id="close-heading" class="home-close__title">Bring it to your next session.</h2>
      <p class="home-close__lede">Running a campaign is free, and so is playing in as many as you like.</p>
      <%= render "pages/cta" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>
</div>
